SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] MaineCare Telehealth Services Provider Licens
 ure Requirements
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			MaineCare Telehealth Services Provider Licensure Requir
 ements\nMaineCare Telehealth Services Provider Licensure Requirements\nSep
  08\, 2026\nAs a reminder\, all providers delivering telehealth services t
 o MaineCare members must be enrolled with MaineCare and must comply with
  MaineCare Benefits Manual\n(MBM) Chapter I\, Section 4: Telehealth Servi
 ces\n.\nChapter I\, Section 4 requires that providers be\n“appropriately
  licensed\, accredited\, certified\, and/or registered in the state where 
 the member is located during the provision of the telehealth service.”\n
 This means that all providers delivering in-person or telehealth services 
 to MaineCare members\, who are in Maine at the time of the service\, must 
 hold appropriate Maine credentials or Interstate Licensure Compacts reco
 gnized by the\nDepartment of Professional and Financial Regulation\n(DPFR)
  or other appropriate organization.\nPursuant to\nMBM\, Ch. I\, Section 1.
 18\nfailure to comply with these requirements can result in the denial o
 f claims or recoupment of payment because services delivered without prope
 r state licensure are not eligible for reimbursement.\nFor questions\, ple
 ase contact your\nProvider Relations Specialist\n.\nhttps://www.maine.gov
 /dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-telehealth-services-provi
 der-licensure-requirements-2026-09-08
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-
 telehealth-services-provider-licensure-requirements-2026-09-08
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
